# Eleven Minutes | EXT | Senegal Pavilion, Courtyard | DAY | lucien, awa, moussa | Get off | He steps off the belt. She answers his mime in perfect French. {moussa} arrives. So does a fine | {lucien} leaves the platform | 5 | crowd=80, props=kora
# The Summer | EXT | Palace Of Electricity, Roof | NIGHT | lucien, awa | Show her the lights | He has a key. The whole fair lit below. She tells him the village is plaster and what a real song is for | | 6 | vfx=illuminated exposition
# The Summer | INT | Pavement Machine Hall | DAY | lucien, gaspard | Be offered a life | The Metro, a wage, a foreman's daughter mentioned in passing. {lucien} says he will think | | 4 | props=machinery
# The Summer | EXT | Seine Embankment | DUSK | lucien, awa | Ask her to stay | He asks. She asks what she would be here, in December. He opens his mouth and has nothing | {lucien} sees the question is his to answer | 6 | water
# The Last Night | EXT | Moving Pavement, Breakdown Point | NIGHT | lucien, awa, moussa, gaspard | Mend it | The belt stops with ten thousand aboard. He goes under with a spanner; she holds the lamp; {moussa} holds back the crowd | | 6 | crowd=400, stunts=under-platform repair, props=lamp+spanner
# The Last Night | EXT | Bordeaux Quay | DAWN | lucien, awa, moussa | Go | A steamer. She has the tickets. He has the kora on his back and no cap | He goes with her | 3 | water, crowd=60, vehicles=steamship, props=kora+tickets
review: authored | 2026-11-12 | written whole; drawn from the 1900 Exposition's moving pavement and colonial pavilions, with invented people
